  "narrative": {
    "intro": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance has $16.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date from 26 awards, with an average award size of $636M and obligations up 23.7% year over year. TriWest Healthcare Alliance received $11B from the Department of Veterans Affairs and $5.6B from the Department of Defense in FY2026 to date. TriWest Healthcare Alliance earns $16.3B in the Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers market and $288M in Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds in FY2026 to date. TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations have risen from $6.7B in FY21 to $16.5B in FY26, passing $7.4B in FY22, $8B in FY23, $8.4B in FY24, and $13.4B in FY25 on the way to the current total. TriWest Healthcare Alliance average award size of $636M reflects the concentration of dollars into relatively few awards. TriWest Healthcare Alliance current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are TriWest Healthcare Alliance's obligations?",
        "body": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance has $16.5B in obligations across 26 awards, producing an average award size of $636M. TriWest Healthcare Alliance receives most dollars from the Department of Veterans Affairs, which accounts for $11B, and the Department of Defense, which accounts for $5.6B. TriWest Healthcare Alliance revenue is concentrated in the Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers market, which accounts for $16.3B. TriWest Healthcare Alliance shows a high concentration of federal revenue in a small number of large awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has TriWest Healthcare Alliance's federal business changed over time?",
        "body": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations rose year over year and are up 23.7% in FY2026 to date. TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations moved from $6.7B in FY21 to $13.4B in FY25 and to $16.5B in FY26. TriWest Healthcare Alliance shows steady increases each fiscal year listed: $7.4B in FY22, $8B in FY23, and $8.4B in FY24. TriWest Healthcare Alliance current FY2026 figures are fiscal year to date and are partial totals."
      }
    ]
  },
